{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7887a8a18473d601a18db7d1533494&lang=en": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix",
      "description": "Position: Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 114-Thrive # of Openings: 1 Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, 12-month, grant-funded Project Coordinator, THRIVE VIA Hendrix. Reporting to the Project Director and Director of Student Well-Being, the Project Coordinator is responsible for day-to-day implementation of THRIVE VIA Hendrix, Hendrix College's SAMHSA-funded suicide prevention, mental health, and substance use disorder initiative. Working under the PD, the PC serves as a liaison to the JED Foundation's JED Campus program and leads training logistics, data collection activities, and lethal means assessments. This role requires strong organizational skills; comfort working across academic, clinical, and student affairs stakeholders; and the ability to manage multiple workstreams independently. Working conditions are office environment with some evenings/weekends for trainings and events, occasional in-state travel to community partners, and travel to a required SAMHSA grantee meeting (Washington, DC) with the PD. Key Responsibilities: JED Campus Liaison: Serve as day-to-day point of contact with the JED Campus Advisor and Team; support JED-related assessments; track progress across four program phases. Outreach & Social Media: Collaborate on outreach campaigns and social media content promoting help-seeking and connectedness; track engagement metrics for reporting. Research & Assessment Support: Support an annual needs assessment; maintain records for quarterly and annual reporting. Gatekeeper Training Logistics: Coordinate scheduling, materials, and attendance tracking for GUIDE, MHFA, and QPR trainings. Crisis, Referral, and Lethal Means Coordination: Support community partner agreements and campus-wide 988 promotion; lead environmental scans for access to lethal means. General Program Administration: Support a transition-to-workforce workshop and other project events; assist with budget tracking, match documentation, and grant compliance. Required and Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in psychology, public health, higher education, social work, communications, or a related field; Master’s degree preferred Experience working with college-age students in a health, educational, or nonprofit setting Familiarity with mental health, suicide prevention, or substance use concepts; gatekeeper certification (QPR, MHFA, ASIST) a plus, or willingness to obtain Experience creating and managing social media or digital campaign content Experience with data collection, survey administration, and basic research tasks Strong written and verbal communication skills, adaptable across student, faculty, administrator, and community-partner audiences Demonstrated ability to coordinate across stakeholders and manage multiple workstreams Preferred: Prior experience with a multi-year initiative and federally-funded grant programs Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application and a resume with contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. This position is grant funded, contingent on continued federal funding and renewable annually through 9/29/2030. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859e9de070f7019e1cdb2d401a10&lang=en": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Position: Custodian Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-FM-Cust # of Openings: 1 Custodian Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, support staff Custodian. Working under the direct supervision of the Custodial Supervisor, the Custodian p rovides routine cleaning of buildings, furniture and equipment on a daily basis and conducts routine housekeeping tasks in accordance with established standards and instruction. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Sweep, mop and scrub floors, stairs (inside and outside buildings) and other surfaces. Must keep all dispensers appropriately filled. Use light and heavy (industrial type) floor machines and attachments. Scrub, strip and wax floors using heavy (industrial type) powered scrubber and buffers. Vacuum rugs/carpets in offices and public areas. Shampoo rugs/carpets periodically using heavy vacuum cleaner and rug shampooing machine. Clean and dust furniture, exhibit cases, pictures, door trim and chalkboards. Clean, equipment and scrubbers and change brushes, pads, rollers, buffers and other attachments. Wash window sills, glass in corridor doors, and clean blinds. Wash and/or clean interior wall s paces while working on ladders. Clean and service lavatories, toilet rooms and restrooms. Collect trash and debris and place in collection area for removal by Facilities personnel. Replace liners in wastebaskets and trash containers. Move heavy furniture, supplies and miscellaneous equipment, as directed. Submit workorders for needed repairs (doors, door checks, furniture lights, faucets, etc.). Must adhere to all safety standards and work practices established by Facilities Management. Perform a number of special projects related to various aspects of Facilities Management. Complete and/or maintain department records and forms relating to the custodial operation. Conduct routine building inspections to assess needs. Performs specialized tasks during adverse weather conditions and college closures. In the event of unscheduled closures due to weather events and/or other circumstances, serves as “essential personnel” for reopening the college. Must complete all required training as scheduled. Perform other duties, as assigned. ESSENTIAL SKILLS: Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions. Ability to bend, stoop, climb ladders, move and/or push/pull equipment. Must be able to lift a minimum of 50 pounds. Must be dependable, punctual and have a good attendance record. Must be able to work overtime and/or weekends, when required. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume and contact information for three professional references. Salary is $12.00 per hour. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78879ea15447f701a163dddbb462a7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mover",
      "description": "Position: Mover Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 110-Mover # of Openings: 1 Mover Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, support staff Mover. Working under the direct supervision of the Moving Supervisor, the Mover p erforms all aspects of moving requests including set-ups, take-downs, and preparation for special events. Directs the work of Movers or other assigned employees. JOB DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform general moving duties and assist other departments when needed. Works closely with requestors and coordinate the movers to ensure adequate coverage for special events in a timely manner. Complete moving/set-up/breakdown work orders and delivery of freight. Operates moving vehicle in conjunction with delivery of freight and performance of moving work order duties. Communicate positively with faculty, staff, and students in completion of duties. Do routine care of all moving vehicles. Deliver housekeeping supplies. Maintains and sets all student room furniture as needed. Assists with all furniture moving on campus. Deliver heavy mail packages and freight deliveries. Maintain a clean and orderly warehouse. Ensure workorders are completed in a timely manner in SchoolDude. Performs specialized tasks during adverse weather conditions and college closures. In the event of unscheduled closures due to weather events and/or other circumstances, serves as “essential personnel” for reopening the college. Must complete all required training as scheduled. Other duties as assigned. ESSENTIAL SKILLS: Ability to read, write and follow oral and written instructions. High School diploma or equivalent. Walking, stooping and climbing for long periods of time. Lifting of objects weighing more than 50 pounds. Ability to withstand extreme hot/cold weather. Operation of heavy equipment. Ability to work safely with hazardous chemicals in a cautious and safe manner. Ability to work overtime and/or weekends. Must be dependable, punctual and have a good attendance record. Must have current Arkansas drivers license. The Facilities Department will contact individuals for interviews based on applications submitted through this page. Due to the volume of applications and interest that we receive, we do ask that you refrain from calling our Facilities Department directly. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. . Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7883ac9d02ffb2019d203a127750ca&lang=en": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Physics",
      "description": "Position: Adjunct Instructor of Physics Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 2026-Physics-Adj # of Openings: 1 Adjunct Instructor of Physics The Department of Physics at Hendrix College seeks applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Physics to teach one section of PHYS 160: Astronomy – an introductory survey course intended for non-science majors, for either semester of the 2026-2027 academic year. The instruction of this course takes place on campus and typically meets for three one-hour sessions per week. Instructors are also expected to provide reasonable office hours to support student learning. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. A master’s degree or higher is required. Applications for the position should include a letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae/resume, transcripts (unofficial) from highest degree earned, and list of three references including email address and phone number. Please email any questions to Dr. Julie Gunderson ( gundersonj@hendrix.edu ), Chair of the Physics Department. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where employees treat each other with respect, dignity, and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a1358052c420ab&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions)",
      "description": "Position: Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 106-Mgmt # of Openings: 1 Assistant or Associate Professor of Economics and Business - Management (2 positions) Hendrix College invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the rank of assistant or associate professor of economics and business specializing in management to begin in August 2027. The successful candidates will work with other Economics and Business faculty to launch a new Business management major which is anticipated to start in August 2027. While we welcome candidates with broad interests in the management field, candidates with interests in sports, healthcare, operations, or supply chain management are particularly encouraged to apply. Primary teaching duties will include introductory and upper-level Business Management courses such as Principles of Management, Organization Behavior, Business Communications, Business Ethics, and upper-level Business Management electives. The normal teaching load is three courses per semester. The terminal degree requirement is a Ph.D. in Business Management or a related field such as Business Administration or Business Analytics; ABD will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are particularly encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching and scholarly interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin October 26, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Gina Bergfeld at bergfeld@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859fa152cc4201a15f59e21a79a4&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Art Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 109-Art # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Art Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of art with an emphasis in 3D art to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach courses in ceramics and 3D art such as wheel throwing, sculpture, 3D design, and mixed media; supervise studio activities, including oversight of kiln operations, studio maintenance, and health and safety protocols; and engage in their professional studio work. Our facilities are excellent with spaces for a variety of studio art disciplines. We are well equipped to support 3D art including a comprehensive ceramics and sculpture studio, foundry area, woodshop, and 3D printers. An MFA in Art or a related field (or equivalent professional experience) is required by the start date; candidates who are ABD at the time of application will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae that includes information about exhibitions and prior teaching experience, a statement of teaching interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at this stage). If unable to upload transcripts as one document, you may email one or both of them to facultyrecs@hendrix.edu. The cover letter should also include a link to an outline portfolio of 15-20 images of your recent work and a link to an online portfolio of no more than 20 images of student work (if available). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Art Department Chair Dr. Rod Miller at miller@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a1358b099324bd&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences)",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 107-Chem # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Chemistry (Pharmaceutical Sciences) Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of chemistry in the area of pharmaceutical chemistry to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will work with other natural science faculty to launch a new Pharmaceutical Sciences major which is anticipated to start in August 2027. They will teach courses in pharmacology and toxicology, medicinal chemistry, and drug discovery and development and also be expected to contribute to the organic chemistry or biochemistry sequence of courses, depending on their area of expertise. The position comes with competitive start-up funding and carries a full-time teaching load of six course equivalents per year, where one course equivalent comprises a lecture section or two lab sections. Doctorate at time of appointment is required, postdoctoral experience is preferred. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching and research interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Chemistry Department Chair Dr. Peter Kett at kett@hendrix.edu , especially if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859ea133541101a13578e7581db4&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics",
      "description": "Position: Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 105-Econ # of Openings: 1 Assistant Professor of Economics and Business – Economics Hendrix College invites applications for a tenure-track position as an assistant professor of economics and business in the area of economics to begin in August 2027. While we welcome candidates with broad interests in the field of economics, candidates with interests in health, environmental, or behavioral economics are particularly encouraged to apply. Primary teaching duties will include introductory and upper-level economics courses such as microeconomics, macroeconomics, statistics, econometrics, economic research, and upper-level economics electives. The normal teaching load is three courses per semester. The terminal degree requirement is a Ph.D. in Economics; ABD will be considered. Celebrated among the country’s leading liberal arts colleges for academic quality, engaged learning opportunities and career preparation, vibrant campus life, and value, Hendrix has been named one of the nation’s Most Innovative Schools in the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings and is featured in Colleges That Change Lives: 45 Schools That Will Change the Way You Think About Colleges. The College seeks to extend its tradition of excellence in teaching and scholarship by attracting faculty who combine mastery of their disciplines with broad intellectual interests and commitment to the aims of a liberal arts college. Candidates who are excited to contribute to our new Via Hendrix curriculum , which combines hands-on work experience with a strong liberal arts education, are particularly encouraged to apply. Applications should include a cover letter addressing the candidate’s interest in teaching in a liberal arts environment, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching interests, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and graduate and undergraduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at this stage). In addition, three letters of recommendation should be requested and sent by e-mail to FacultyRecs@hendrix.edu . Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs . Review of materials will begin October 26, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to Gina Bergfeld at bergfeld@hendrix.edu , particularly if you are interested in more information about the position in advance of applying. Hendrix is a distinguished liberal arts college located in Conway, Arkansas, thirty miles from Little Rock at the foothills of the Ozark Mountains. The College, affiliated with the United Methodist Church, has a strong commitment to excellence in teaching liberal arts and career preparation. Hendrix College is an equal opportunity employer, and all applications will be considered without regard to race, gender, disability, sexual orientation, national origin or any other characteristic specified by law. The College is committed to maintaining an atmosphere of civility and respect for all students, faculty, and staff. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a78859fa152cc4201a15f01b2054ea7&lang=en": {
      "title": "Part-Time Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Position: Part-Time Public Safety Officer Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 108-PSO # of Openings: 1 Public Safety Officer (Part-Time) Hendrix College is seeking a part-time, 12-month support staff position. Reporting to the Director of Public Safety, the Public Safety Officer ensures the safety of persons and property on the Hendrix campus and helps manage various emergency situations. The anticipated part-time hours for this position are 8pm to 3:30am, Wednesday-Saturday. POSITION RESPONSIBILITIES: Patrol campus buildings and grounds to prevent or respond to conduct that is a violation of law and/or College expectations to include incidents of theft, vandalism, fire or fire hazards, disorderly conduct, parking violations, etc. Ensure buildings are locked and unlocked as appropriate. Inspect life safety equipment, which includes checking locks, lighting, fire extinguishers and alarms to confirm they are in working order. Report any public safety incidents and unusual or hazardous conditions on campus to appropriate officials (i.e., inoperative alarms, discharged or defective fire extinguishers, broken windows, etc.). Investigate complaints made by faculty, staff, or students on campus. Investigate traffic accidents on campus. Assist local law enforcement, fire, and other emergency personnel as needed. Foster lasting relationships and trust with students, staff, and faculty through open and effective communication. Provide public safety services such as parking and traffic direction, crowd control, and the like, for special events. Issue parking citations and report traffic violations. Assist police with investigations on campus. Provide visitors directions and general Hendrix College information. Complete all required paperwork on campus incidents and public safety activities. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Public Safety. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Looking for friendly, motivated, enthusiastic candidates. Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent plus experience in customer service. Knowledge of first aid techniques; CPR certification is a plus. Experience working as a member of a team and building relationships with those you serve and support. In-House training provided. Required Skills: Familiarity with relevant laws; basic knowledge of fire prevention; valid driver’s license; ability to deal effectively with a wide range of individuals, in some instances under stressful, dangerous and/or emergency conditions; ability to handle emergency situations calmly and efficiently; demonstrated integrity; must have the physical ability to perform all job duties. Writing skills that allow for comprehensive reporting of incident response and engagement with members of the College community. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume with contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. You can learn more about the College's commitment to diversity and inclusion by reviewing our statement: https://www.hendrix.edu/diversity/statement/. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7883a8a184746e01a1a24994730716&lang=en": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Retail Management and Campus Hospitality",
      "description": "Position: Executive Director of Retail Management and Campus Hospitality Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 115 # of Openings: 1 Executive Director of Retail Management and Campus Hospitality Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, 12-month Executive Director of Retail Management and Campus Hospitality. Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Operations/Chief Financial Officer, the Executive Director functions as the College's chief hospitality and retail executive, leading multiple business units through strategic planning, financial stewardship, operational excellence, customer service innovation, and staff development. The Executive Director of Retail Management and Campus Hospitality provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the College's auxiliary retail enterprises, including Dining Services, The Burrow, the Campus Market (Spirit Store and Convenience Store), Vending Services, Concessions, Conferences and Events, Catering, and Post Office. This position is responsible for developing a cohesive campus hospitality strategy that enhances the student experience, supports enrollment and retention initiatives, strengthens institutional branding, and generates sustainable auxiliary revenues. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Leadership Develop and implement a comprehensive strategic plan for all retail and hospitality operations. Create a long-term vision that aligns auxiliary operations with the College's strategic plan. Identify and develop new revenue-generating opportunities. Benchmark operations against peer and aspirational institutions. Prepare annual and multi-year business plans for each operating unit. Lead capital improvement planning for retail and dining facilities. Foster a culture of innovation, hospitality, entrepreneurship, and continuous improvement. Establish a staffing model which shares employees across the operating units. Other duties as assigned. Financial Management Direct responsibility for the financial performance of all retail enterprises. Responsibilities include: Develop annual operating and capital budgets. Monitor monthly financial performance. Analyze profit and loss statements. Develop revenue forecasts. Establish pricing strategies to yield a net profit for revenue producing areas. Monitor labor costs. Manage food costs without sacrificing quality. Manage inventory investment. Improve operating margins. Recommend capital investments. Responsible for annual revenues and expenses associated with: Residential Dining The Burrow Campus Market Spirit Store Convenience Store Vending Concessions Conferences Catering Post Office Dining Services Leadership Provide executive oversight for all campus dining operations based on being “destination” locations. Responsibilities include: Residential dining Meal plans Menu strategy Food quality Nutrition initiatives Student satisfaction Dining hours Sustainability initiatives Vendor management Food safety compliance The Burrow Lead the transformation of The Burrow into the College's premier campus gathering place. Responsibilities include: Brand development Menu strategy Programming with Student Affairs Evening activities Specialty beverages Retail food offerings Student engagement Technology integration Customer experience Financial performance Campus Market Provide executive leadership for the integrated Campus Market consisting of the Spirit Store and Convenience Store. Responsibilities include: Retail Merchandise Campus apparel Gifts Alumni merchandise Graduation merchandise Athletic merchandise Online store Convenience Store Fresh grab-and-go meals Grocery items Snacks Beverages School supplies Personal care products Residence hall essentials Technology accessories Develop strategies to maximize customer traffic through extended operating hours, seasonal promotions, and integrated merchandising. Conferences and Events Provide strategic oversight for all conference and event operations. Responsibilities include: Campus calendar (internal/external) Summer conferences Corporate events Weddings Camps Community rentals Internal events Space scheduling Event contracts Revenue development Customer service standards Develop and execute strategies to maximize year-round utilization of campus facilities. Catering Provide executive leadership for the College's catering enterprise. Responsibilities include: Internal catering External catering Catering sales Menu development Event coordination Food production Quality assurance Revenue growth Customer satisfaction Concessions Lead all concession operations supporting: Athletics Performing arts Campus events Community events Special programs Develop premium concession offerings that enhance customer experience while maximizing profitability. Vending Services Oversee campus vending operations. Responsibilities include: Product selection Healthy options Fresh food vending Technology upgrades Vendor contracts Inventory management Revenue optimization Equipment replacement planning Ensure vending serves as the College's after-hours food and beverage solution while complementing dining operations. Marketing and Brand Development Develop a unified brand strategy for all retail operations. Responsibilities include: Marketing plans Promotions Loyalty programs Social media Student engagement Alumni promotions Community outreach Digital communications Retail merchandising Seasonal campaigns Collaborate closely with the Office of Communications to maintain institutional brand consistency. Customer Experience Establish a campus-wide hospitality culture. Develop measurable service standards for: Dining Retail Conferences Catering Campus visitors Alumni Parents Guests Measure customer satisfaction through surveys, mystery shopper programs, and operational metrics. Personnel Leadership Provide leadership for all professional, full-time, part-time, and student employees within the division. Responsibilities include: Hiring Performance management Staff development Succession planning Student employment Leadership development Training Employee engagement Safety Scheduling Develop a student leadership program offering progressive roles such as Shift Lead, Supervisor, and Manager, creating meaningful experiential learning opportunities. Technology and Innovation Lead technology initiatives including: Point-of-sale systems Mobile ordering Self-service kiosks Digital menu boards Inventory management Online retail Business intelligence dashboards Event management software Customer analytics Mobile payment solutions Leverage data analytics to improve operational performance and decision-making. Compliance and Risk Management Ensure compliance with all applicable federal, state, and local regulations, including: Health and food safety requirements Alcohol service regulations ADA accessibility Employment laws Cash handling standards Emergency preparedness Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Hospitality Management, Retail Management, Food Service Management, Finance, Higher Education Administration, or a related field or any combination of education and experience that would provide the executive knowledge required at this level. Seven to ten years of progressively responsible leadership experience in hospitality, auxiliary services, retail management, dining services, conference services, or a comparable multi-unit operation. Demonstrated experience managing complex budgets and financial operations. Experience supervising multiple departments and professional staff. Proven record of revenue growth, operational improvement, and customer service excellence. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in Business Administration (MBA), Hospitality Management, Higher Education Administration, or a related discipline. Experience in higher education auxiliary services. Experience managing self-operated dining and retail enterprises. Knowledge of conference and event management, including catering. Experience with POS, inventory, and retail management systems. Experience leading organizational change and business transformation. Core Competencies Strategic Planning Financial and Business Acumen Communication and Relationship Building Hospitality Leadership Retail Operations Revenue Generation Customer Experience Management Organizational Leadership Data Analytics and KPI Management Marketing and Merchandising Team Development Project Management Operational Excellence Change Management Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) The Executive Director will be evaluated annually on: Financial Net operating margin by business unit Revenue growth Budget performance Food cost percentage Labor cost percentage Inventory turnover Gross margin return on investment (GMROI) Student Experience Student dining satisfaction Meal plan participation Burrow utilization Campus Market transaction growth Net Promoter Score (NPS) Service response times Operational Excellence Conference occupancy and utilization Catering revenue growth Spirit merchandise sales growth Convenience store sales per labor hour Concession profitability Vending up time and sales performance Strategic Outcomes Growth in external conference revenue Increase in auxiliary net contribution to the College Student employee retention and leadership development Cross-unit collaboration and innovation Successful implementation of strategic initiatives This position is intentionally designed as a business executive role , not a traditional food service director. The Executive Director is accountable for a diversified portfolio of auxiliary enterprises, operating with the expectation that each unit contributes to the College's financial sustainability while enhancing recruitment, retention, campus life, and institutional reputation. This strategic orientation aligns the position with senior leadership responsibilities appropriate for reporting directly to the Vice President for Finance and Operations/CFO. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application and a resume with contact information for three professional references. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7885aca18473fa01a1c0ffb8a9701a&lang=en": {
      "title": "Part-Time Catering Assistant",
      "description": "Position: Part-Time Catering Assistant Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 116 # of Openings: 1 Catering Assistant (Part-time) Hendrix College is seeking two part-time, 9-month, support staff Catering Assistants. Reporting to the Catering Manager, the Catering Assistant a ssists the Catering Manager with events, including preparation, execution, supervision, and cleanup. Assures all details are managed and accounted for. Could at times assume responsibility for conducting the entire event, when the event is small. POSITION RESPONSIBILITIES: Utilizes events sheets to confirm and assist that all details and supply gathering are complete well in advance of event Participates in and oversees events and assigns duties to catering pool staff including but not limited to packing supplies, setting up, serving, cleaning, and returning supplies to proper location Completes department inventories of supplies Other duties as assigned POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Position requires working some weekends and nights, and at times split shifts Able to stand on feet for long periods of time and lift 25 pounds EDUCATION: Must have high school equivalent and be able to read and follow directions EXPERIENCE: Catering experience is a plus SKILLS: Ability to multi-task, take and give direction, and interact positively with guests Organized, keen attention to detail Self-starter with willingness to help in all areas as needed. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a resume with contact information for three professional references. The hourly rate of pay is $12.07. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. You can learn more about the College's commitment to diversity and inclusion by reviewing our statement: https://www.hendrix.edu/diversity/statement/. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://www.hendrix.edu/humanresources/jobs.aspx?gnk=job&gni=8a7885aca18473fa01a1c11379af77d9&lang=en": {
      "title": "Front of House Supervisor (PM)",
      "description": "Position: Front of House Supervisor (PM) Location: Conway, AR Job Id: 117 # of Openings: 1 Front of House Supervisor (PM) Hendrix College is seeking a full-time, 10-month Front of House Supervisor. Reporting to the Executive Director of Retail Management and Campus Hospitality, the Front of House Supervisor m anages a team of employees to maintain a friendly, hospitable atmosphere, premium food service, and cleanliness in the Front of the House. POSITION RESPONSIBILITIES: Manages the workflow of employees by creating schedules, delegating tasks, communicating the cafeteria’s goals, and providing constant feedback. Interviews and hires candidates for the Front of the House area. Assesses the work performance of employees and identifies areas that need improvement. Trains and on boards new hires to make sure they understand their responsibilities. Plans, orders, and executes special events to break the monotony for our students, faculty, and staff. Create and build props and items for events. Oversees and decorates in the dining room and servery for each event and most holidays. Ensures there is a sufficient number of cashiers, line servers, dining room attendants, and beverage attendants to cover all shifts and fills in that position as needed. Creates an Excel report for all credit card transactions and submits it to the Business Office each month. Collects data on inventory, purchases, labor, and sales to compile a report that figures CPP weekly. Inventory and order what is needed for Front of the House twice a week. Acts as manager-on-duty as needed. Hires, schedules, and supervises work study students for the cafeteria. Make monthly schedules of groups, times, rooms reserved, and number of guests (if given) for separate departments; update as needed. Other duties as assigned. POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: Experience in customer service management required. Experience in food service preferred. Knowledge of Excel, Word, and Outlook preferred. EXPERIENCE: Supervisory experience (interviewing, scheduling, managing). SKILLS: Must have good communication and organizational skills. Must be able to work in a high stressed, fast paced environment. Must be a good listener and have leadership skills. GOALS : Communicate and improve where is needed. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications should include a letter of application and a resume with contact information for three professional references. The hourly rate of pay is $13.56. Applications can be submitted at www.hendrix.edu/jobs. Questions about this position can be submitted to hr@hendrix.edu. Hendrix College strives to maintain an environment free from discrimination and harassment, where members of the Hendrix Community treat each other with respect, dignity and courtesy. The College adheres to the principle of equal educational and employment opportunity without regard to age, race, color, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, or national origin. You can learn more about the College's commitment to diversity and inclusion by reviewing our statement: https://www.hendrix.edu/diversity/statement/. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    }
